                "{\"score\": 3, \"reasoning\": \"All four panels are present, but tiny text and truncated/repeated tick labels undermine readability. The final chain is connected but elongated rather than compact and spills outside its panel into the heat-capacity panel. Histograms contain multiple temperature-dependent curves, though their strongly overlapping low-Q distributions show much weaker folding separation than the reference. The response curve varies with temperature, but plots C_v/T^2 rather than C_v and marks T*=0.367 below the sampled temperatures without clear transition support. The free energy is dominated by repetitive spikes rather than interpretable basins and barriers; its reported zero barrier and single mode do not establish a credible folding transition. The reference also has spiky free energy, but the agent adds substantial readability and consistency problems.\"}"
